0..70 Comment "// A theory\'s operation written at its type: `oper next : T => T`, the"
71..142 Comment "// value-function alias, is the operation of its domain and its result,"
143..220 Comment "// `(_ : T) --> T`, as `functor-pair.gandr`\'s record signature writes `next`;"
221..296 Comment "// so is the thunk of curried arrows it stands for, which a judgment writes"
297..366 Comment "// for more than one input, `oper add : +U (M -> M -> -F M)`, since a"
367..443 Comment "// parenthesised list there opens the judgment\'s own port group. A port at a"
444..514 Comment "// builtin type the theory does not declare reads that type, so `read`"
515..591 Comment "// returns an `Integer`. A model gives each as the function it writes for an"
592..605 Comment "// operation."
607..668 Comment "/// A counter, the theory of `functor-pair.gandr`\'s signature"
669..733 Comment "/// `#{ type T, zero : T, next : T => T, read : T => Integer }`."
